FAMILY LAW: the apex obstruction is PURE SOS (p=1 mod4) vs SIGN x SOS (p=3 mod4). Isolates Borsuk-Ulam to p=3 mod4.
On the maximal-real-subfield Gaussian periods of Q(zeta_p) (the "de Moivre" periods, degree d=(p-1)/2):

  p= 3 (n= 6, d=1, 3 mod4): trivial (depth 1), value 0.
  p= 5 (n=10, d=2, 1 mod4): AM-GM-of-2 = (a-b)^2 = +5 = +disc(Q(sqrt5)). *** PURE SOS *** (a literal square) -> SOS+Brouwer.
  p= 7 (n=14, d=3, 3 mod4): AM-GM-of-3 = (a+b+c)(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ca) = (-1)(7) = -7 = -disc(Q(sqrt-7)).
                            *** SIGN x SOS *** -> needs the Borsuk-Ulam odd-degree/sign certificate.
  (d>=4 closed-form not computed here; the GENERAL mechanism is the discriminant SIGN = p mod 4, rigorous via HYP-3220.)

MECHANISM (rigorous, HYP-3220): disc(Q(sqrt(+-p))) = +p if p=1 mod4 (real, SOS) ; = -p if p=3 mod4 (imaginary, sign).
=> p=1 mod 4 (n=10,26,...): obstruction is a positive multiple of an SOS -> SOS+Brouwer route closes it.
   p=3 mod 4 (n=14,22,...): obstruction = (fixed negative trace sign) x (SOS) -> Borsuk-Ulam (free Z_2) certifies the sign.
n=14 is the FIRST nontrivial p=3 mod4 apex = the first genuine Borsuk-Ulam / imaginary-quadratic case (and h(-7)=1, a UFD).
